    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "b51edf707b71a5416b797b47530e6ced4698946c9cd2d094f819cb73a75dec97",
      "text": "After breakfast, take a sightseeing tour of Baños and visit the waterfalls.\n\nBaños sits in a valley near Tungurahua Volcano.\n\nThe volcano rises to 5,016 m.\n\nThe town itself lies at about 1,826 m, has a population of around 20,000 and an average annual temperature of about 20 °C.\n\nThe area is known for its hot springs and range of outdoor activities.\n\nOptions include rafting, rock climbing, canyoning, ziplining, hiking, mountain biking and bungee jumping.\n\nAfter a short tour of the town, follow the waterfall route.\n\nThe itinerary includes Agoyán, Manto de la Novia (“Bridal Veil”) and Pailón del Diablo (“Devil's Cauldron”).\n\nThe route includes a walk along the canyon.\n\nAt Bridal Veil Falls, you take a cable car.\n\nYou can also ride the famous Swing at the End of the World.\n\nZiplining over the Pastaza Canyon is available as an optional activity.\n\nZiplining costs USD 15 per person.\n\nIn the afternoon, transfer to Riobamba.\n\nThe evening is free.\n\nStay at Casa Real (4-star).\n\nBreakfast is included.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-32of1ztisn",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      }
    },
